prompt:
A real photograph of the Senhora do Monte viewpoint above Lisbon on a September Sunday at sunset, in a tall vertical picture, caught as it happens, as a walker would take it with a good phone camera. Taken with a 24 mm lens at standing eye height from the top of the stone steps that lead up to the viewpoint, looking across the terrace towards the city and the river below, everything in sharp focus. Low golden sunlight from the left and a warm orange sky; the textures of real white limestone paving, worn stone, iron, bark, terracotta roof tiles, water, cotton, denim and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young man from the front, the second shows him from his side: his face, his wavy dark-brown hair, his short stubble, his build, his height and his clothes, the royal-blue hooded sweatshirt with its red band across the chest, the white t-shirt, the cream scarf with small blue embroidered flowers, the dark-blue jeans and the white canvas sneakers, stay exactly as in them.

Every surface in the picture is plain: the bags are plain single colours, the benches are plain wood, the boats are plain white, and the clothes are plain cloth. Each object stands clearly on its own, with a band of bare paving or bare sky around it, so that the eye can tell at once where everything is.

The picture is built in three bands, from the bottom edge to the top edge.

THE FOREGROUND, along the bottom of the picture:
- the last stone steps of the climb rise from the bottom edge of the picture, with an old iron handrail on their right;
- the young man of the reference pictures stands on the top step, on the left of the middle, seen whole from his head to his white sneakers; his body is turned in three-quarter view towards the right of the picture; he is bent forward, both hands on his knees, completely out of breath, his cheeks red, his mouth open;
- beside him, on the right, a small old lady of eighty in a black cardigan and a grey skirt walks briskly past him up the last step, a full plastic shopping bag in each hand, a leek sticking out of one of them; she turns her head towards him with a kind, amused smile as she passes.

THE MIDDLE OF THE PICTURE, the terrace, from left to right:
- on the left, a big old tree with a twisted trunk shades a wooden bench, where a young couple sits looking at the view;
- in the centre, on the white limestone paving, a young musician sits on a folding stool playing an acoustic guitar, its open black case at his feet with a few coins in it; a small brown dog lies beside the case;
- on the right, a low white stone wall runs along the edge of the terrace, with an old black iron street lamp at its end; a seagull stands on the wall.

THE CITY, across the upper third of the picture:
- below the viewpoint, the whole city spreads out in the golden light: a sea of terracotta roofs and white and pale-yellow houses tumbling down the hills;
- on the left, on its hill, the stone castle with its square towers and walls;
- in the middle distance, the white dome and two bell towers of a large church;
- beyond the roofs, the wide river shines gold, with two small white sailing boats on it, and on the right the long red suspension bridge crosses it;
- above, a warm orange sky fading to pale blue at the top, the sun low and round just above the far hills.

The terrace is calm and open: between the people, the same bare white paving, and the whole city beyond.
